 7. ⚖️ DOJ probes Lewandowski 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Corey Lewandowski, Susie Wiles and Natalie Harp arrive with then-candidate Donald Trump in Fayetteville, N.C., in 2024. Photo: Evan Vucci/AP The Justice Department is investigating longtime Trump ally Corey Lewandowski over allegations that he profited personally while advising the Department of Homeland Security, The Wall Street Journal and N.Y. Times report. 

 Why it matters: Lewandowski was President Trump's first campaign manager in 2016 and top aide to former Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, who was fired in March. It's a rare instance of a Trump ally being investigated during his second term. Trump told reporters yesterday when asked about the reported probe: "I don't know exactly what it is ... All I know is, I want my people to be honest. And if they're not going to be honest, they have to be prosecuted."

 A lawyer for Lewandowski, Adam Trigg, said Lewandowski "has not been contacted by the Justice Department regarding any investigation, and he denies any wrongdoing when he was proudly serving his country in a voluntary capacity." Keep reading (NYT gift link). 

 
 
